# CodeMind 2.0 — Architecture Overview (Detailed Edition)

**A self-hosted, multi-language, graph-based code-understanding and code-generation system — now with a built-in natural-language brain, deterministic math, policy-driven safety, and a hardened web-search subsystem.**

> **Document version:** 2.0 — describes **CodeMind 2** (source markers `v84`–`v89`, plus the final hardening pass).
> This document **replaces** the 1.0 overview. The two describe different generations of the system; where 1.0 and 2.0 disagree, 2.0 is the one checked against the current source. Section 2 lists every material difference.

> **Confidentiality & IP Notice**
> Every mechanism below was checked against the real implementation (`CodeMind.py`, `codemind_brain_dual.py`, `build_graph_cache.py`, `search.py`, `linguistic_safety.py`). To protect the project's intellectual property, this document **explains what each part does and why it exists**, but it deliberately **contains no source excerpts, no loss/reward coefficients, no tuned thresholds, no regular expressions, no training data, and no model weights**. Scale figures (layer counts, widths, expert counts, context lengths) are given because they are needed to understand the design. The repository, not this document, is the source of truth.

